    (shortDescription) piml is a data serialization format designed to be exceptionally human-readable and writable, while maintaining a clear and unambiguous structure for machine parsing. Spec v1.2.0 is implemented by three official libraries - go-piml, piml.js and piml.net - plus a tree-sitter grammar, all validated against one shared compliance suite.
    (date) 2026-09-10
    (image) /images/projects/piml.webp

